# --- User-specified ignores ---
# Top-level directories
# Note: macOS APFS is case-insensitive at the filesystem layer but git pattern
# matching is case-sensitive — list every case variant present in the repo.
# `ResoucePool` is intentionally spelled with one 'r' to match the actual
# on-disk directory name (do not "correct" without renaming the directory first).
PROCESS/
Process/
process/
ResoucePool/

# Directories whose name contains "Design" (any case)
**/Design*/

# Hidden files (name starts with a dot)
.*

# Files whose name contains Draft / Drafts / Email / Review / 评估 / STD / bom
# Note: Git pattern matching is case-sensitive on all platforms (even on macOS APFS
# which is case-insensitive at the filesystem layer). List every case variant we
# encounter in practice to avoid silent gaps.
**/*Draft*
**/*Drafts*
**/*draft*
**/*drafts*
**/*Email*
**/*email*
**/*EMAIL*
**/*Review*
**/*review*
**/*REVIEW*
**/*评估*
**/*STD*
**/*std*
**/*bom*
**/*BOM*

# Stray 0-byte "Icon\r" files (filename ends with carriage return)
# Generated by an unknown tool on 2026-06-09; safe to delete locally.
# Pattern uses `?` to match the single trailing CR byte.
Icon?
**/Icon?